<title>FRANCE: Dior 1996 net attrib 1.26 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Dior 1996 net attrib 1.26 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   1,255  vs	   1,638</p>
<p>    Net					    3,576  vs	   4,657</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		    15.20    up six percent</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		 4,943  vs	   4,666</p>
<p>    Turnover				    32,353  vs	  30,796</p>
<p>NOTE - Dior SA, which controls 41.7 percent of LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton, gave its results in a statement.</p>
<p>It said its 1996 results include 558 million francs of exceptional charges, reflecting a reclassification of assets with LVMH and the impact of LVMH's sale of a third of its stake in British groups Guinness Plc.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
